> Checking geometry and work

>> A three-dimensional diagonal bowl

Use curvature (2,2,2), centre (4,-2,1) and start (10,10,10). Nesterov uses
eta=.05 and up to 5000 updates; coordinate methods and CG use their native
budgets of 1000 epochs/steps. Randomized blocks have two coordinates and seed 42.
These declared budgets are not a speed ranking. Every table includes the returned
gradient norm and callback counts, and the plot samples only gradient requests.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/opt_coordinate_diagonal.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace o = dm::optim;
  o::QuadraticObjective                 f({2, 2, 2}, {4, -2, 1});
  std::vector<double>                   start{10, 10, 10};
  o::NesterovAcceleratedGradientOptions n;
  n.step_size      = .05;
  n.max_iterations = 5000;
  o::RandomizedBlockCoordinateDescentOptions b;
  b.block_size = 2;
  std::vector<o::OptimizationRun> runs;
  runs.push_back(
      o::trace_optimize<o::DifferentiableFunction>(f, o::NesterovAcceleratedGradient(n), start));
  runs.push_back(o::trace_optimize<o::DifferentiableFunction>(f, o::CoordinateDescent(), start));
  runs.push_back(
      o::trace_optimize<o::DifferentiableFunction>(
          f, o::RandomizedBlockCoordinateDescent(b), start));
  runs.push_back(o::trace_optimize<o::DifferentiableFunction>(f, o::ConjugateGradient(), start));
  const std::vector<std::string> labels{"Nesterov", "cyclic", "blocks", "CG"};
  o::optimization_comparison(f, runs, labels, "gradient")
      .title("Diagonal bowl: derivative requests")
      .size(850, 490)
      .save_svg("build/opt_coordinate_diagonal.svg");
  for (std::size_t i = 0; i < runs.size(); ++i)
    std::print(
        "{}\n\n{}\n\n{}\n\n",
        labels[i],
        runs[i].summary().to_md(7),
        runs[i].trace.counts().to_md(0));
}
```
