>> Rotate a stiff bowl, then couple five coordinates

The first test rotates eigenvalues (2,200) through pi/4 without changing their
condition number. Axes no longer align with independent directions. The second
uses five diagonal curvatures (2,4,8,16,32) plus 30 times the all-ones rank-one
matrix, with a known centre. Coupling makes partial updates interact even without
an explicit rotation. Nesterov uses eta=.005 here; the other declared controls
remain the same. No external dataset is needed: the known minimizers and analytic
curvature let the experiment isolate geometry. Different dimensions and callback
mixes prevent a universal wall-time conclusion from these traces.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/opt_coordinate_geometry.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace o = dm::optim;
  o::QuadraticObjective rotated({2, 200}, {0, 0}, 0, std::numbers::pi / 4),
      coupled({2, 4, 8, 16, 32}, {4, -2, 1, 0, .5}, 30);
  o::NesterovAcceleratedGradientOptions n;
  n.step_size      = .005;
  n.max_iterations = 5000;
  o::RandomizedBlockCoordinateDescentOptions b;
  b.block_size = 2;
  const std::vector<std::string>   labels{"Nesterov", "cyclic", "blocks", "CG"};
  std::vector<dm::graphics::RPlot> plots;
  for (auto* f : {&rotated, &coupled}) {
    std::vector<double>             start(f == &rotated ? 2 : 5, 10);
    std::vector<o::OptimizationRun> runs;
    runs.push_back(
        o::trace_optimize<o::DifferentiableFunction>(*f, o::NesterovAcceleratedGradient(n), start));
    runs.push_back(o::trace_optimize<o::DifferentiableFunction>(*f, o::CoordinateDescent(), start));
    runs.push_back(
        o::trace_optimize<o::DifferentiableFunction>(
            *f, o::RandomizedBlockCoordinateDescent(b), start));
    runs.push_back(o::trace_optimize<o::DifferentiableFunction>(*f, o::ConjugateGradient(), start));
    plots.push_back(
        o::optimization_comparison(*f, runs, labels, "gradient")
            .title(
                f == &rotated ? "Rotated two-dimensional bowl" : "Coupled five-dimensional bowl"));
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < runs.size(); ++i)
      std::print(
          "{} {}\n\n{}\n\n",
          f == &rotated ? "rotated" : "coupled",
          labels[i],
          runs[i].summary().to_md(7));
  }
  dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1, 2)
      .add(plots[0])
      .add(plots[1])
      .size(1100, 490)
      .fit_panels()
      .save_svg("build/opt_coordinate_geometry.svg");
}
```
