>> Rosenbrock: curvature changes along the path

For f=(1-x0)^2+100*(x1-x0 squared)^2, the minimum zero is at (1,1).
The same direction mechanisms now see a curved, varying valley, started at
(-1.2,1). Nesterov uses .001 and a budget of 20000 updates; coordinate and CG
budgets remain 1000. A low final objective is checked alongside the gradient norm,
not inferred from a visually flat convergence curve. Finite budgets and selected
settings do not establish a global ordering among the algorithms.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/opt_coordinate_rosenbrock.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace o = dm::optim;
  o::SmoothBenchmark                    f("rosenbrock");
  std::vector<double>                   start{-1.2, 1};
  o::NesterovAcceleratedGradientOptions n;
  n.step_size      = .001;
  n.max_iterations = 20000;
  o::RandomizedBlockCoordinateDescentOptions b;
  b.block_size = 2;
  std::vector<o::OptimizationRun> runs;
  runs.push_back(
      o::trace_optimize<o::DifferentiableFunction>(f, o::NesterovAcceleratedGradient(n), start));
  runs.push_back(o::trace_optimize<o::DifferentiableFunction>(f, o::CoordinateDescent(), start));
  runs.push_back(
      o::trace_optimize<o::DifferentiableFunction>(
          f, o::RandomizedBlockCoordinateDescent(b), start));
  runs.push_back(o::trace_optimize<o::DifferentiableFunction>(f, o::ConjugateGradient(), start));
  const std::vector<std::string> labels{"Nesterov", "cyclic", "blocks", "CG"};
  o::optimization_comparison(f, runs, labels, "gradient")
      .title("Rosenbrock: derivative requests")
      .size(850, 490)
      .save_svg("build/opt_coordinate_rosenbrock.svg");
  for (std::size_t i = 0; i < runs.size(); ++i)
    std::print(
        "{}\n\n{}\n\n{}\n\n",
        labels[i],
        runs[i].summary().to_md(7),
        runs[i].trace.counts().to_md(0));
}
```
